&lt;p style=&quot;margin-left:.5pt;&quot;&gt;
	Peter Symonds College is fully committed to the highest standards of health and safety for our students, staff, and visitors. Following a recent inspection by Winchester City Council on 2nd March 2026, we were disappointed to receive a rating of &amp;#39;1&amp;#39;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin-left:.25pt;&quot;&gt;
	The issues identified could be rectified swiftly, and the College has taken rapid and robust action. This has included refresher training for all staff, and further strengthening our internal quality assurance processes. The College is also continuing its existing programme of significant capital investment in its catering facilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;margin-left:.7pt;&quot;&gt;
	Following a follow-up visit on 12th March 2026, Winchester City Council&amp;#39;s Environmental&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
	Health Officer expressed satisfaction with the rapid and robust nature of our improvements. We have formally requested a re-rating inspection and are confident that our facility now exceeds the standards required for the &amp;#39;Good&amp;#39; and &amp;#39;Very Good&amp;#39; ratings (Levels 4 and 5) that the College has historically maintained.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
	The safety and wellbeing of our community remain our absolute priority. We look forward to welcoming the inspectors back to formalise our updated rating shortly.&lt;/p&gt;
